# Git — no push without explicit request

Applies to all `github.com/omcrgnt/*` work.

## Rule

**Do not run `git push`, `git push --tags`, or any command that publishes commits/tags to a remote** unless the user explicitly asks in the current message or in a user rule for that action.

## Allowed without a push request

- `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, local branch operations
- Local `git commit` when the user asked to commit (see commit user rule)
- Local `git tag` when the user asked to tag
- Prepare push commands for the user to run
- `gh pr create` only after user asked to create a PR **and** push is required — still confirm push if not explicitly requested

## When the user asks to push

Push only what they asked for (branch, tags, `--force` only if explicitly requested; never force-push to main/master unless explicitly requested).

## After local commits/tags

Tell the user what is ready locally and offer the exact `git push` / `git push origin <tag>` commands — do not run them unless asked.
